member.remarks:
Employs a numerically stable, iterative recurrence without direct factorial or power computation:


f_0 = 1, \quad f_k = f_{k-1} \cdot \left(\frac{-x}{k}\right) = \frac{(-x)^k}{k!}



\text{term}_k = \frac{f_k}{k} = \frac{(-x)^k}{k \cdot k!}



The iteration terminates when |\text{term}_k| < \text{tolerance} \cdot |S_k|.
